n't want to put in the  work to get there so it's just really  hard to invest in any of the characters  I felt like I liked Deadshot the most Oh  Will Smith  I thought the Joker was really bad I  thought Halle was fine but it's just  that most of it is edited in just the  most snappy ways I mean articles have  surfaced about the post-production off  to it so what I'm speculating here maybe  actually has some merit but it's  basically like everything is just cut so  there's no actual conversation like a  lot of it is just a scene with a  character saying one line I'm gonna cut  to the next thing and they just keep  doing that it's like it seems like it's  less common in that movie for individual  characters to actually talk to each  other and it's mostly just one character  saying something and then it cut to  someone else and then it cut to someone  else and it's like they're not  conversing which is just very odd  editing but I do want to mention that I  absolutely love DC I prefer DC of a  model I have a Batman tattoo and I read  more DC Comics than Marvel Comics I just  don't like the movies DC I'm making at  the moment and I really wish that they  would make better ones inside came out  on ps4 I  talk about this on my last month's  highlights but seriously plan side it is  great that's all I'm gonna say just play  it and then I sell sausage potty which  is moved from seth rogen uh this one's  weird to talk about it's not a bad movie  because the pacing is good the narrative  makes sense but it was a comedy and i  didn't laugh once in that movie I feel  like there are a few moments mostly  relating to some creative puns where I  was like huh but I didn't actually laugh  out loud even once because it seemed  like the butt of most of the jokes was  food swearing like legitimately a lot of  the jokes in that movie what just this  character is swearing a lot that's funny  I understand other people finding it  funny but this is a movie that's not for  me it's not a bad movie just on a moon  for me I also reviewed a game called  valley which is made by the same people  who might slender the arrival it's an  adventure game it is there's lots of  like speedrunning platforming moments  which is like it's like a first-person  sonic and in the parts where you're  going really fast it's super cool but  then it kind of slows you down a lot of  the time to make you explore this wall  that it's very hard to get invested in  it's not very long the combat is really  boring it's definitely pretty but the  mechanics are kind of nonsensical and  forced and the story is just it has  interesting a law but it's just you have  no stakes or stakeholders because the  valley is empty except you so it just  felt like it was pointless I'll leave a  link to my review on that one also I  don't want to talk about it too much  because I feel like most people haven't  heard of it so probably don't care  Deus Ex came out I haven't had a chance  to play too much of that unfortunately  but from why I have played I really like  it it's very intuitive I love the south  options and it's also quite hard which I  mean I suck at stealth games anyway so I  say they're all hard but it's just the  way the environments in structured  provide a very unique kind of challenge  and anyone who enjoys stealth games will  really like Deus Ex though of course you  don't have to play it stealth believe  you don't want to you can just go in at  guns blazing so it gives you that  creativity and freedom as well which is  really cool and then last but not least  I sell Kubo which is a stop-motion film  that is just really lovely who I was  surprisingly laid out like a video game  I like there are levels and bosses which  I wonder if they drew inspiration from  video games because I kept thinking that  and that's actually always really cool  to see in a movie but there were parts  of it that didn't really make sense some  things that happened you know what  justified or explained very well but I  feel like I could ignore those things  based on one thinking that it was very  pretty and two it was just so pleasant  to watch also in like sound design and  voice acting was great and the  principles or I guess just the fairytale  aspects of it were just really lovely  it's also impossible not to appreciate  the craft in that kind of movie I saw a  facebook video that was like a  time-lapse of them building some of  these characters and one of the bosses  which is just huge it's way too open  people and that is just so impressive I  think it took them five years to make  the movie and it looks great and I  believe that was it the stuff that I  checked out in August alrighty I will  see you guys next time

